./md-review-records/2026-08-09-git-gatekeeper-design/codex-hunt-good.md.stderr.log:140:    95	In version 1, between screening and push, **no judgment refusal remains** — this stage is deterministic construction and recording; infrastructure failures (`workspace-io-error`, `network-down`) can still arise here and are safely resubmittable. In v1 the check set *is* construction itself, so guarantee 2 binds the checks that exist — construction — to the exact pushed bytes; it gains content as checks are added. That is the growth point, not a hole: when a test suite exists, the tests run here; when the boss gates an artifact class, its review-evidence check runs here (the request format grows its evidence field then, not before).
