142:{"parentUuid":"988ae787-d513-4af9-ba86-28f046f78827","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6cf0bce6-877a-4b97-9459-514ab1f94d64","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XCj9njyf3rvrq3yfoPv6p2","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/nedlern/.claude/projects/-home-nedlern-Projects-nedschorus/memory/md-no-hard-wrap.md"}]},"uuid":"8b5cf741-a75b-4e83-a67d-21edd1e2ddae","timestamp":"2026-08-11T20:11:57.756Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/nedlern/.claude/projects/-home-nedlern-Projects-nedschorus/memory/md-no-hard-wrap.md","content":"---\nname: md-no-hard-wrap\ndescription: \"Don't hard-wrap paragraphs at ~80 characters in MD files the user will read or edit — one line per paragraph, let the editor soft-wrap\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd\n  modified: 2026-08-11T20:11:57.737Z\n---\n\nIn MD files meant for the user to read or edit, don't hard-wrap paragraphs at ~80 characters. Write each paragraph or bullet as one long line and let the editor soft-wrap.\n\n**Why:** Hard line breaks inside paragraphs make the file harder for him to edit (his words, 2026-08-11, on the sanity-checker draft — which was then reflowed on his direction).\n\n**How to apply:** One line per paragraph, bullet, or heading in prose MD files. This is about breaks inside a paragraph, not structure — keep normal blank lines between paragraphs and normal list/heading markup. See also [[mac-file-link-format]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"988ae787-d513-4af9-ba86-28f046f78827","session_id":"d9eda3ec-c327-4154-a2c1-ab5796f1ce65","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster","sessionId":"29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd","version":"2.1.227","gitBranch":"choirmaster"}
144:{"parentUuid":"bcc352bd-8f53-4f1c-8211-6bfebb633152","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6cf0bce6-877a-4b97-9459-514ab1f94d64","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KB45Z8ZyVzaPPBsxceaXi5","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"449ee090-565d-4e20-a770-c56160e51b69","timestamp":"2026-08-11T20:12:01.188Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bcc352bd-8f53-4f1c-8211-6bfebb633152","session_id":"d9eda3ec-c327-4154-a2c1-ab5796f1ce65","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster","sessionId":"29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd","version":"2.1.227","gitBranch":"choirmaster"}
146:{"parentUuid":"9122704f-493c-4bdb-9a6d-7ef237dcc197","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6cf0bce6-877a-4b97-9459-514ab1f94d64","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJ4xwAmhEp3DyGRwZAiS9Z","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/nedlern/.claude/projects/-home-nedlern-Projects-nedschorus/memory/mac-file-link-format.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"782bb971-cf60-4c19-9806-b2ffeed08908","timestamp":"2026-08-11T20:12:10.224Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/nedlern/.claude/projects/-home-nedlern-Projects-nedschorus/memory/mac-file-link-format.md","content":"---\nname: mac-file-link-format\ndescription: \"Link ned-box files as clickable markdown links in the file:///Volumes/nedhome/... form (his Mac mounts the nedhome SMB share)\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd\n  modified: 2026-08-11T20:12:10.201Z\n---\n\nWhen handing the user a link to a file on this machine (ned-box), make it a clickable markdown link whose target replaces the `/home/nedlern/` prefix with `file:///Volumes/nedhome/`. Example: for `/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md`, write `[x.md](file:///Volumes/nedhome/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md)`.\n\n**Why:** He reads from his Mac, where the Samba share `nedhome` (exporting `/home/nedlern`, server `ned-box`) is kept mounted at `/Volumes/nedhome`; `file://` links open the file directly, while `smb://` links only mount and open the enclosing folder. A bare URL pasted as plain text isn't reliably clickable in his terminal — markdown link syntax is (his direction, 2026-08-11).\n\n**How to apply:** Use the clickable `[name](file:///Volumes/nedhome/...)` form when the point is for him to click and read a file — this applies to any link handed to him, smb:// fallbacks included. Keep plain repo-relative paths in durable artifacts (commits, issues), since `/Volumes/...` paths are meaningless on ned-box itself. If the share ever fails to resolve, fall back to `smb://ned-box.local/nedhome/...` (IP fallback: 10.0.1.39). See also [[md-no-hard-wrap]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":15,"newStart":1,"newLines":15,"lines":[" ---"," name: mac-file-link-format","-description: \"When giving the user a link to a file on ned-box, use the file:///Volumes/nedhome/... form (his Mac mounts the nedhome SMB share)\"","+description: \"Link ned-box files as clickable markdown links in the file:///Volumes/nedhome/... form (his Mac mounts the nedhome SMB share)\""," metadata: ","   node_type: memory","   type: feedback","   originSessionId: 29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd","-  modified: 2026-08-11T20:08:41.459Z","+  modified: 2026-08-11T20:12:10.201Z"," ---"," ","-When handing the user a clickable link to a file on this machine (ned-box), use the Mac-mounted-share form: replace the `/home/nedlern/` prefix with `file:///Volumes/nedhome/`. Example: `/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md` → `file:///Volumes/nedhome/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md`.","+When handing the user a link to a file on this machine (ned-box), make it a clickable markdown link whose target replaces the `/home/nedlern/` prefix with `file:///Volumes/nedhome/`. Example: for `/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md`, write `[x.md](file:///Volumes/nedhome/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md)`."," ","-**Why:** He reads from his Mac, where the Samba share `nedhome` (exporting `/home/nedlern`, server `ned-box`) is kept mounted at `/Volumes/nedhome`; `file://` links open the file directly, while `smb://` links only mount and open the enclosing folder. (Approved 2026-08-11.)","+**Why:** He reads from his Mac, where the Samba share `nedhome` (exporting `/home/nedlern`, server `ned-box`) is kept mounted at `/Volumes/nedhome`; `file://` links open the file directly, while `smb://` links only mount and open the enclosing folder. A bare URL pasted as plain text isn't reliably clickable in his terminal — markdown link syntax is (his direction, 2026-08-11)."," ","-**How to apply:** Use the `file:///Volumes/nedhome/...` link when the point is for him to click and read a file. Keep plain repo-relative paths for everything else (commits, issues, durable artifacts), since `/Volumes/...` paths are meaningless on ned-box itself. If the share ever fails to resolve, fall back to `smb://ned-box.local/nedhome/...` (IP fallback: 10.0.1.39).","+**How to apply:** Use the clickable `[name](file:///Volumes/nedhome/...)` form when the point is for him to click and read a file — this applies to any link handed to him, smb:// fallbacks included. Keep plain repo-relative paths in durable artifacts (commits, issues), since `/Volumes/...` paths are meaningless on ned-box itself. If the share ever fails to resolve, fall back to `smb://ned-box.local/nedhome/...` (IP fallback: 10.0.1.39). See also [[md-no-hard-wrap]]."]}],"originalFile":"---\nname: mac-file-link-format\ndescription: \"When giving the user a link to a file on ned-box, use the file:///Volumes/nedhome/... form (his Mac mounts the nedhome SMB share)\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd\n  modified: 2026-08-11T20:08:41.459Z\n---\n\nWhen handing the user a clickable link to a file on this machine (ned-box), use the Mac-mounted-share form: replace the `/home/nedlern/` prefix with `file:///Volumes/nedhome/`. Example: `/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md` → `file:///Volumes/nedhome/agents/choirmaster/docs/drafts/x.md`.\n\n**Why:** He reads from his Mac, where the Samba share `nedhome` (exporting `/home/nedlern`, server `ned-box`) is kept mounted at `/Volumes/nedhome`; `file://` links open the file directly, while `smb://` links only mount and open the enclosing folder. (Approved 2026-08-11.)\n\n**How to apply:** Use the `file:///Volumes/nedhome/...` link when the point is for him to click and read a file. Keep plain repo-relative paths for everything else (commits, issues, durable artifacts), since `/Volumes/...` paths are meaningless on ned-box itself. If the share ever fails to resolve, fall back to `smb://ned-box.local/nedhome/...` (IP fallback: 10.0.1.39).\n","userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9122704f-493c-4bdb-9a6d-7ef237dcc197","session_id":"d9eda3ec-c327-4154-a2c1-ab5796f1ce65","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/nedlern/agents/choirmaster","sessionId":"29d66917-9767-47cb-a221-d4876d8014cd","version":"2.1.227","gitBranch":"choirmaster"}
