md-review-records/2026-08-12-attack-split-experiment/inputs/context-fast-handoff-design-at-0890848.md:45:The supervisor's poll never touches the transcript: it stats the handoff file and stamps its heartbeat, nothing more. The transcript is read only by the Stop hook, once per turn boundary, and only from the end — the newest assistant record is all that matters, so the hook reads a 256KB tail and doubles the window until it finds that record. Measured on a 5.8MB transcript: 0.3ms, against 23ms for a whole-file parse, and the gap widens as a session grows because the tail read does not scale with file size.
