md-review-records/2026-08-12-attack-split-experiment/gatekeeper-fresh-eyes-codex.log:158:The gate workflow, policy, credential plumbing, action pins, and relevant ownership rules form the control plane. A proposed change to them requires explicit boss approval and is verified using the old trusted policy. Candidate-controlled workflows are never used as the gate. `pull_request_target`-style execution of submitted code is prohibited.
md-review-records/2026-08-12-attack-split-experiment/gatekeeper-fresh-eyes-codex.log:164:- **Wrong local branch:** Separate worktrees prevent shared-index damage. The gate lands a pinned SHA, not “whatever this branch now means.” Direct pushes to `main` fail server-side.
md-review-records/2026-08-12-attack-split-experiment/gatekeeper-fresh-eyes-codex.log:168:- **Agent crash:** Once intake pins the SHA, no client process is needed. The reconciler continues the request.
md-review-records/2026-08-12-attack-split-experiment/gatekeeper-fresh-eyes-codex.log:173:- **Force-pushed or deleted source branch:** The gate-owned pinned ref remains authoritative.
md-review-records/2026-08-12-attack-split-experiment/gatekeeper-fresh-eyes-codex.log:212:- “Same content” was interpreted as the same tree while a check actually depends on commit parents, commit message, author, timestamp, tags, or shallow-history depth.
